 \begin{lemma}[coverage]\label{lem:coverage}
-R3 audits every served job of identities younger than $L$ rounds (age counted from the first offer) whenever the round's audit count covers them. Under overload, age groups are served newest first; within the focal identity's group of $n$ jobs, of which $s$ are its own, the number audited is hypergeometric with $k' = \min\{n, \max(0, k - H)\}$ draws, $H$ being the fresh jobs of strictly newer identities.
