+A buyer of computation can check only a sample of delivered jobs, and a sanctioned provider can return at once under a new identity. We study a repeated procurement market with noisy delivery, costly exact audits, refunds, finite bans, and free identity replacement, without entry fees, identity certification, or collateral. For the uniform-audit baselines B2 and B3 with refund-and-ban enforcement and no bonds, free replacement makes the ban costless, because replacement restores eligibility bef
+We report four findings. First, pooled over the six markets, R3 and C$^*$ are ``\site{abs_q1_cat}'' within a pre-set margin of $\pm\const{0.05}$ (C$^*$ minus R3 under the D2+H3 attacks: \site{abs_q1_est}); treated as a sample of markets, the per-market D2+H3 differences give an exploratory $t$ interval of [\site{abs_ml_lo}, \site{abs_ml_hi}], so this analysis does not establish the ordering beyond these markets, and the second attack family returned the first family's winner in \site{abs_x7_sam
